@startuml deployment-architecture
title Link — Deployment Architecture (Docker Compose)

node "Host machine" {

  node "docker compose" as compose {

    node "app container\n(next: standalone build)" as app {
      artifact "Node.js 22 alpine" as node
      artifact "Next.js 15 server :3000" as next
      artifact "entrypoint:\ndrizzle-kit migrate → start" as entry
    }

    database "postgres container\n(postgres:16-alpine)" as pg {
      folder "pgdata (named volume)" as vol
    }
  }

  cloud "Reverse proxy\n(Caddy / Traefik / nginx)\nTLS termination — optional,\nrecommended" as proxy
}

actor Curator
actor Visitor

Curator --> proxy : HTTPS
Visitor --> proxy : HTTPS /share/<token>
proxy --> app : HTTP :3000

app --> pg : postgres://…\n(DATABASE_URL, internal network)

note right of pg
  healthcheck: pg_isready
  app depends_on:
    condition: service_healthy
end note

note bottom of app
  Env vars (.env):
  DATABASE_URL
  BETTER_AUTH_SECRET
  BETTER_AUTH_URL
  NODE_ENV=production

  Migrations run automatically at
  startup before server starts.
end note

note bottom of compose
  docker compose up -d
  = full MVP deployment
end note

@enduml
